; Tutorial_4_Track_Job_Leads.inix -- JobTrail: a status brought up to date, a job added, notes kept, and the people linked to a job.

[about]
Title=4 - Track Job Leads
Intro=JobTrail, a job search kept as linked tables: an interview's outcome recorded, a new opening added, a note kept, and from a job to the contact and documents linked to it.
Setup=DbDo is open.
Homework=Replace one sample job with a real lead of your own.

[step]

Say=One want: a job search in one place, with nothing forgotten.
Key=
Hear=

[step]

Say=Alt plus Control plus D, D for DbDo, opens it or brings it forward.
Key=Alt+Control+D
Hear=DbDo
Hear=DbDo ready

[step]

Say=JobTrail is a template for exactly that. Its records are samples, plainly named as samples, to show the shape before your own go in.
Key=Alt+Shift+D
Hear=Template Databases dialog
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=I choose JobTrail and press Enter. It opens on actions, newest first, so the last thing done is the first thing heard.
Key=Enter
Hear=2026-09-24, Follow up on the Accessibility Analyst interview, awaiting reply, Row 1 of 7
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Control plus T, Choose Table, lists its tables: jobs, contacts, actions, documents and stories. I choose jobs.
Key=Control+T
Hear=Choose Table dialog, actions
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Enter.
Key=Enter
Hear=jobs, 4 records, no filter, sorted by employer, title
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Four openings, each at a different stage. I move to the status column of the Accessibility Analyst job.
Key=Right Arrow
Hear=status, interviewing
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Status has fixed values, so Control plus F2, Pick Value, offers them and nothing is mistyped.
Key=Control+F2
Hear=status: list box, interviewing, 3 of 7
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Down Arrow twice to offer, and Enter. F2 would edit the cell as free text instead, as F2 renames a file in Windows.
Key=Enter
Hear=status, offer
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Control plus N, N for New, adds a record, and focus goes to its first field.
Key=Control+N
Hear=New record
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=I fill employer, title and status with F2. Shift plus A, Say Added, says when it was added.
Key=Shift+A
Hear=added: today at 3:40 PM
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=A planned misstep: Control plus D deletes a record, D for Delete, and asks first. Escape answers no.
Key=Control+D
Hear=Delete this record? No button
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Escape keeps it. Notes hold what does not fit a column. Alt plus Shift plus N, Edit Notes, opens them in a box of their own.
Key=Alt+Shift+N
Hear=Notes: edit, multiline
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=I type a line about the opening, and Control plus Enter keeps it. Shift plus N says it back.
Key=Shift+N
Hear=Heard about it from a former colleague; apply by Friday.
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Tags work the same way: Alt plus Shift plus T to edit, Shift plus T to hear, single words such as remote, to filter by later. Alt plus Shift plus U edits the posting's web address.
Key=
Hear=

[step]

Say=Now the links. Up Arrow to the Accessibility Analyst job. Shift plus R, Say Related, says what it leads to, changing nothing.
Key=Shift+R
Hear=contacts 1, docs 2
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Alt plus Right Arrow goes into the related records.
Key=Alt+Right Arrow
Hear=contacts: 1 related record
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=The hiring manager, linked as the contact for this job.
Key=Down Arrow
Hear=Pat, Rivera, Example Widgets Company (sample employer)
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Alt plus Left Arrow comes back, as a browser goes back.
Key=Alt+Left Arrow
Hear=jobs, Example Widgets Company (sample employer), Accessibility Analyst
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=JobTrail also keeps its own questions as scripts. Control plus Shift plus I, Invoke Script, lists them; Today shows the actions due, oldest first.
Key=Control+Shift+I
Hear=Invoke Script dialog, Today
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Escape, for now. When the samples have shown the shape, delete them and add your own.
Key=
Hear=

[step]

Say=What this walk taught. I name the command; the reader gives the key.
Key=
Hear=

[step]

Say=Pick a fixed value.
Key=
Hear=Control plus F2

[step]

Say=Add a record.
Key=
Hear=Control plus N

[step]

Say=Say what a record leads to.
Key=
Hear=Shift plus R

[step]

Say=Go into the related records.
Key=
Hear=Alt plus Right Arrow
